Well, {ma kau} marks an indirect question and in this usage there seems to =
be nothing either indirect or a question.=A0 "Any" in English is a context =
leaper universal quantifier.=A0 Placed within the scope of a negation (incl=
uding a conditional antecedent) or a question (a probably some others) it f=
unctions as a universal over the whole (outside the question or negation or=
 conditional). Provided some conditions are met (slightly different in each=
 case), it functions equally well as a particular quantifier within the the=
 complex.=A0=20

"I any boy comes, the girls will be happy" =3D either "If some boy comes, a=
ll the girls will be happy" or "For every boy x, if x comes the girls will =
be happy"=A0 (note, this will not work with "If any boy comes, the girls wi=
ll dance with him", since the condition is that the scope of the "any" is c=
onfined to the antecedent.=A0 This has to be "For every boy x, if x comes, =
all the girls will dance with x".=A0 The best way to do this in Lojban is i=
n some dispute.)=A0=20

"Do you have anything" =3D either "Do you have something?" or "For every x,=
 do you have x?"
"I don't have anything" =3D either "It is not the case I have something" or=
 "For every x, it is not the case I have x"


